---
import Sheet from '../layouts/Sheet.astro';
import RegistrationMarks from '../components/RegistrationMarks.astro';
---

<Sheet
  title="About SkyKPI | Precast and AEC Marketing and Association Management"
  description="SkyKPI is a small marketing and association management firm for the precast and AEC world. The client list stays small on purpose."
  path="/about/"
  sheet="A-400"
  sheetName="About"
>
  <!-- QUIET OPEN -->
  <section class="section sheet open">
    <RegistrationMarks />
    <div class="container open__inner">
      <p class="tag">Sheet A-400 &middot; About</p>
      <h1>A small firm, on purpose.</h1>
      <hr class="dimline" aria-hidden="true" />
      <p class="lede open__identity">
        SkyKPI LLC is a boutique marketing and association management firm
        serving the precast concrete and AEC industries nationwide from its
        base in Frankfort, Illinois.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE STORY -->
  <section class="section sheet sheet--mist story">
    <div class="container story__grid">
      <div>
        <p class="tag reveal">The story</p>
        <h2 class="reveal">Why this firm exists</h2>
        <hr class="dimline reveal" aria-hidden="true" />
      </div>
      <div class="reveal">
        <p>
          I built SkyKPI because of two problems I kept watching from the
          inside. Trade associations run by one overloaded director, where
          everything lives in one person's head. And industry marketing handed
          to outside agencies that learn precast on the client's dime. I had
          lived both, and the fix looked the same from every angle: a small
          team that already knows the industry.
        </p>
        <p>
          We still run trade associations in the precast and AEC world today.
          That seat is where the marketing work gets its fluency.
        </p>
        <p>
          I started the firm with my wife, Caroline. She left her career as a
          nurse to build it with me, and she has become a true professional in
          this industry in her own right.
        </p>
        <p>
          In 2026 we grew beyond the two of us and brought on our first
          employees. When you work with SkyKPI, the people you meet are the
          people doing the work.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE GRANDFATHER RULE -->
  <section class="section sheet creed">
    <RegistrationMarks />
    <div class="container creed__inner">
      <p class="tag reveal">Standing rule</p>
      <blockquote class="creed__quote reveal">
        <p>&ldquo;Pigs get fat, hogs get slaughtered.&rdquo;</p>
      </blockquote>
      <p class="tag tag--dim reveal">My grandfather's rule</p>
      <hr class="dimline dimline--center reveal" aria-hidden="true" />
      <p class="dim reveal creed__meaning">
        It is an old saying, but he is the reason it stuck with me. Appetite
        is healthy and greed gets you killed. It still runs this firm. We
        grow with discipline, take on work we can do well, and turn down the
        rest.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- HOW WE DECIDE -->
  <section class="section sheet sheet--mist decide">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="tag reveal">General notes</p>
      <h2 class="reveal">How we decide</h2>
      <hr class="dimline reveal" aria-hidden="true" />
      <ul class="decide__list">
        <li class="reveal">
          <span class="tag tag--dim">G1</span>
          <p>
            The client list stays small on purpose. We turn down work that
            does not fit, because the right clients matter more than more
            clients.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li class="reveal">
          <span class="tag tag--dim">G2</span>
          <p>
            We embed in a client's business and treat it like our own. We
            decline engagements where marketing is treated as a box to check.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li class="reveal">
          <span class="tag tag--dim">G3</span>
          <p>
            Relationships come first. In this industry the people are the
            market, and the model is built on knowing them for decades, not
            for a campaign.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li class="reveal">
          <span class="tag tag--dim">G4</span>
          <p>
            Quality over quantity, applied to everything: the client list,
            the work, the pace.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li class="reveal">
          <span class="tag tag--dim">G5</span>
          <p>
            Client work stays confidential. No names, no case studies, no
            borrowed credit.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHERE -->
  <section class="section sheet where">
    <div class="container where__grid">
      <div>
        <p class="tag reveal">Location</p>
        <h2 class="reveal">Based in Frankfort. Working nationwide.</h2>
        <hr class="dimline reveal" aria-hidden="true" />
      </div>
      <div class="reveal">
        <p>
          The firm is based in Frankfort, Illinois, south of Chicago, in the
          corridor where a lot of this country's precast gets made and moved.
          The team works from more than one place, and the client list has
          never been local.
        </p>
        <p>
          Our service area is the United States. Where you are has no bearing
          on whether we fit.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a class="where__link" href="mailto:hello@skykpi.com">hello@skykpi.com</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="section sheet cta">
    <div class="container cta__inner">
      <p class="tag reveal">Sheet A-500</p>
      <h2 class="reveal">See if we fit.</h2>
      <hr class="dimline dimline--center reveal" aria-hidden="true" />
      <div class="reveal">
        <a class="btn" href="/contact/">Start the conversation</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Sheet>

<style>
  .open {
    padding-top: calc(var(--header-h) + var(--space-section));
  }

  .open__inner {
    max-width: 46rem;
  }

  .open__identity {
    max-width: 36rem;
  }

  .story__grid,
  .where__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 5fr 6fr;
    gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4.5rem);
    align-items: start;
  }

  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .story__grid,
    .where__grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  /* The grandfather rule: the page's centerpiece */
  .creed__inner {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .creed__quote {
    margin: 1.5rem 0 1rem;
    max-width: 46rem;
  }

  .creed__quote p {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 4.6vw, 3.4rem);
    line-height: 1.1;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .creed__meaning {
    max-width: 32rem;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  .decide__list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 2rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    max-width: 44rem;
  }

  .decide__list li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 3rem 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 1.1rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline-on-ink);
  }

  .decide__list li:last-child {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline-on-ink);
  }

  .decide__list p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .where__link {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--teal);
  }

  .cta__inner {
    text-align: center;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
  }
</style>
